    RowBox[{
    "Print", "[", \
"\"\<\!\(\*StyleBox[\"Lambda\",FontWeight->\"Bold\",FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, \
0.4000152590218967, 0.2]]\)\!\(\*StyleBox[\" \
\",FontWeight->\"Bold\",FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.4000152590218967, \
0.2]]\)\!\(\*StyleBox[\"vacuum\",FontWeight->\"Bold\",FontColor->RGBColor[0.6,\
 0.4000152590218967, 0.2]]\)\!\(\*StyleBox[\" \
\",FontWeight->\"Bold\",FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.4000152590218967, \
0.2]]\)\!\(\*StyleBox[\"equations\",FontWeight->\"Bold\",FontColor->RGBColor[\
0.6, 0.4000152590218967, \
0.2]]\)\!\(\*StyleBox[\":\",FontWeight->\"Bold\",FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, \
0.4000152590218967, 0.2]]\)\!\(\*StyleBox[\" \
\",FontWeight->\"Bold\",FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.4000152590218967, 0.2]]\) \
The equations are \!\(\*SubscriptBox[\(R\), \(\[Mu]\[Nu]\)]\) = \
\[CapitalLambda] \!\(\*SubscriptBox[\(g\), \(\[Mu]\[Nu]\)]\). They are \
expressed as \!\(\*FractionBox[SubscriptBox[\(R\), \(\[Mu]\[Nu]\)], \
SubscriptBox[\(g\), \(\[Mu]\[Nu]\)]]\) = \[CapitalLambda] when \
\!\(\*SubscriptBox[\(g\), \(\[Mu]\[Nu]\)]\) \[NotEqual] 0, and \
\!\(\*SubscriptBox[\(R\), \(\[Mu]\[Nu]\)]\) = 0 when \
\!\(\*SubscriptBox[\(g\), \(\[Mu]\[Nu]\)]\) = 0. The \
\!\(\*SubscriptBox[\(g\), \(\[Mu]\[Nu]\)]\) matrix used is a diagonal matrix. \
Since off-diagonal \!\(\*SubscriptBox[\(R\), \(\[Mu]\[Nu]\)]\) equations \
rarely appear, almost all the equations are expressed by dividing out \
\!\(\*SubscriptBox[\(g\), \(\[Mu]\[Nu]\)]\).\>\"", "]"}], ";"}], 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
