Cell[BoxData["\<\"We can easily see that \[ScriptCapitalA](t) = \
\\!\\(\\*SuperscriptBox[\\(c\\), \\(2\\)]\\) is simply a rearrangement of the \
continuity equation. Thus, the 4-branch a(t) formula is the solution to the \
Friedmann equations.\"\>"], "Print",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.9991000055570383`*^9, 3.999332274695044*^9, {3.999332378529189*^9, 
